#: src/printable/components/printable-nightmare-sudoku-page/printable-nightmare-sudoku-page.tsx
msgid "The {PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE} puzzles print {PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE} to a page, sized so a chain crossing the whole grid still fits comfortably on one sheet. Full solved grids close the booklet, which matters more here than at the easier tiers — a single missed elimination partway along a chain compounds quickly, and a printed answer key catches it. The measured spread behind these claims lives in the <0>sudoku difficulty rating guide</0>."
msgstr "The {PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE} puzzles print {PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE} to a page, sized so a chain crossing the whole grid still fits comfortably on one sheet. Full solved grids close the booklet, which matters more here than at the easier tiers — a single missed elimination partway along a chain compounds quickly, and a printed answer key catches it. The measured spread behind these claims lives in the <0>sudoku difficulty rating guide</0>."

#: src/difficulty/components/infinity-sudoku-page/infinity-sudoku-page.tsx
msgid "The best-known Infinity grids have pages of their own, each playable, printable and solved step by step by the engine: <0>AI Escargot</0>, <1>Golden Nugget</1>, <2>Platinum Blonde</2>, <3>Everest</3>, <4>Kolk</4> and <5>Silver Plate</5>."
msgstr "The best-known Infinity grids have pages of their own, each playable, printable and solved step by step by the engine: <0>AI Escargot</0>, <1>Golden Nugget</1>, <2>Platinum Blonde</2>, <3>Everest</3>, <4>Kolk</4> and <5>Silver Plate</5>."

#: src/how-to-play/components/how-to-play-page/how-to-play-page.tsx
msgid "The grid itself never changes: nine rows, nine columns and nine boxes, eighty-one cells in total. What changes from puzzle to puzzle is only which cells start filled and which digits they hold, and it is that starting layout of givens that determines how much logic is needed to reach the one valid solution."
msgstr "The grid itself never changes: nine rows, nine columns and nine boxes, eighty-one cells in total. What changes from puzzle to puzzle is only which cells start filled and which digits they hold, and it is that starting layout of givens that determines how much logic is needed to reach the one valid solution."

#: src/printable/components/printable-sudoku-page/printable-sudoku-page.tsx
msgid "The large-print set uses the same Easy-tier logic as the booklet above, but at {PRINTABLE_LARGE_PRINT_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE} puzzles per page instead of {PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE}, so every cell and digit prints noticeably bigger. It suits low-vision solvers, classroom handouts read from a distance, and anyone who finds the standard grid cramped on paper. See the <0>large print sudoku page</0> for printing tips and the on-screen alternative, or the <1>sudoku for seniors</1> guide for the full comfort-focused rundown."
msgstr "The large-print set uses the same Easy-tier logic as the booklet above, but at {PRINTABLE_LARGE_PRINT_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE} puzzles per page instead of {PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE}, so every cell and digit prints noticeably bigger. It suits low-vision solvers, classroom handouts read from a distance, and anyone who finds the standard grid cramped on paper. See the <0>large print sudoku page</0> for printing tips and the on-screen alternative, or the <1>sudoku for seniors</1> guide for the full comfort-focused rundown."

#: src/difficulty/components/infinity-sudoku-page/infinity-sudoku-page.tsx
msgid "The other tiers are defined by the techniques they require. Infinity is defined by reputation, measured: a puzzle qualifies only if independent raters have published an SE rating of {minimumRatingLabel} or higher for it. Most of the {infinityCorpusSize} come from a 2011 snapshot of the hardest-puzzle database the sudoku-solving community maintains; the rest are the named classics, taken from the forum threads and publications where they first appeared. Before the set is packed into the app, a Dancing Links exact-cover solver and a bitmask solver both confirm that every grid has exactly one solution."
msgstr "The other tiers are defined by the techniques they require. Infinity is defined by reputation, measured: a puzzle qualifies only if independent raters have published an SE rating of {minimumRatingLabel} or higher for it. Most of the {infinityCorpusSize} come from a 2011 snapshot of the hardest-puzzle database the sudoku-solving community maintains; the rest are the named classics, taken from the forum threads and publications where they first appeared. Before the set is packed into the app, a Dancing Links exact-cover solver and a bitmask solver both confirm that every grid has exactly one solution."

#: src/printable/components/printable-newbie-sudoku-page/printable-newbie-sudoku-page.tsx
msgid "The PDF opens with a cover page stating the puzzle and page counts, moves into {PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE} puzzles printed {PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE} to a page, and closes with every solved grid on the final pages so answers never sit next to an unsolved puzzle. Every grid is drawn with vector lines and the standard PDF Helvetica font, so it stays sharp at any print size and never depends on a scanned image. Our published sample of {sampleSize} Newbie boards measures SE {seRatingRange} — numbers the <0>sudoku difficulty rating guide</0> measures directly rather than assumes."
msgstr "The PDF opens with a cover page stating the puzzle and page counts, moves into {PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_SIZE} puzzles printed {PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE} to a page, and closes with every solved grid on the final pages so answers never sit next to an unsolved puzzle. Every grid is drawn with vector lines and the standard PDF Helvetica font, so it stays sharp at any print size and never depends on a scanned image. Our published sample of {sampleSize} Newbie boards measures SE {seRatingRange} — numbers the <0>sudoku difficulty rating guide</0> measures directly rather than assumes."

#: src/printable/components/printable-newbie-sudoku-page/printable-newbie-sudoku-page.tsx
msgid "The printable Newbie Sudoku booklet is a free PDF of {clueCount}-clue puzzles where every blank is reachable with a full house or a naked single — a property each puzzle was checked for before it went into the PDF. It is the booklet to hand a first-time solver, a classroom just learning the rules, or anyone who wants a puzzle that never demands a second guess."
msgstr "The printable Newbie Sudoku booklet is a free PDF of {clueCount}-clue puzzles where every blank is reachable with a full house or a naked single — a property each puzzle was checked for before it went into the PDF. It is the booklet to hand a first-time solver, a classroom just learning the rules, or anyone who wants a puzzle that never demands a second guess."

#: src/printable/components/printable-infinity-sudoku-page/printable-infinity-sudoku-page.tsx
msgid "The puzzles are printed exactly as they were published, with no reshuffling, so you can compare your grid with the originals discussed on the <0>hardest sudoku puzzles</0> page. They print {PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE} to a page with room for a full set of pencil marks, which you will need: at this level most solvers keep every candidate written in and test chains on a separate sheet. The final pages hold the completed grids, so you can check a long line of reasoning without having to finish it first."
msgstr "The puzzles are printed exactly as they were published, with no reshuffling, so you can compare your grid with the originals discussed on the <0>hardest sudoku puzzles</0> page. They print {PRINTABLE_BOOKLET_PUZZLES_PER_PAGE} to a page with room for a full set of pencil marks, which you will need: at this level most solvers keep every candidate written in and test chains on a separate sheet. The final pages hold the completed grids, so you can check a long line of reasoning without having to finish it first."

